# Database (SQLite by default — change to postgres:// for production)
DATABASE_URL="file:./dev.db"

# ── Shared deployment keys (e.g. one key for a whole class) ──────────────────
#
# By default every user brings their own key and it never leaves their browser.
# To have the deployment supply the key instead, set these two:
#
#   1. The key itself — server-only, never sent to a browser:
# OPENAI_API_KEY="sk-..."
#   Also supported: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY,
#   GROQ_API_KEY, TOGETHER_API_KEY, OPENROUTER_API_KEY, AZURE_API_KEY,
#   CUSTOM_API_KEY
#
#   2. Which providers to offer with that key (public — not a secret):
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SHARED_KEY_PROVIDERS="openai"
#
# Both are read at BUILD time for the NEXT_PUBLIC_ one (it is inlined into the
# bundle), so rebuild after changing it. Calls for a covered provider are routed
# through the server automatically — `NEXT_PUBLIC_BROWSER_STORAGE=0` is NOT
# required, and setting it additionally moves run history from each user's
# IndexedDB to the server database.
#
# A user who enters their own key in Settings always uses it instead of the
# shared one. Local providers (Ollama / LM Studio) are unaffected — they always
# run browser-direct, since only the user's own machine can reach them.
#
# WARNING: this makes /api/* usable by anyone who can load the site. Put an
# access gate in front of the deployment, and set a hard spend cap in your
# provider's dashboard — that cap is the only limit that always holds.
